{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>What shall we say to my lord.</b> Even regarding the first money — <b>what shall we speak</b> — regarding the second money — what shall we justify — regarding the goblet." "<b>Both we and he in whose hand the goblet is found.</b> But what does this come to teach us? After all, even those who did not sin became slaves — all the more so Benjamin himself, in whose hand the goblet was found! Rather, one may answer: because earlier they said, ״אשר ימצא אתו מעבדיך ומת, וגם אנחנו נהיה לאדוני לעבדים״. When his brothers saw that it was found in Benjamin's hand, they said: <b>both we</b> are slaves, as we said; <b>and he in whose hand the goblet is found</b> — he shall be nothing but a slave, for they feared lest they kill him. The order of the perasha of Mikeyts is complete."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:36.710770875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}